# The git hooks are bash scripts run on every developer's machine and in CI. A CRLF
# checkout breaks bash on the first line (`set: pipefail: invalid option name`), so
# every commit would be refused; keep them LF whatever core.autocrlf says.
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Same reason, same failure: a CRLF checkout puts a `\r` on the shebang line, and the
# kernel then looks for an interpreter named `bash\r`. `scripts/seed.sh` is the one a
# developer runs first, so it would be the first thing to break on a Windows checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf
